<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.323 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.323 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.3 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due November 6 was 3.323 percent, just up from from 3.321 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.1 billion of 175-day T-bills due January 29, 1998 was 3.711 percent, down from 3.725 percent last week, and on C$1.0 billion of 364-day T-bills due August 6, 1998 was 4.193 percent, down from 4.26 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$525 billion three-month, C$100 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$800 million of C$4.8 billion bills due August 14. (Details follow)  </p>
